<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Colonna family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Colonna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Colonna family is a Roman noble family prominent in the politics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> from the twelfth century. Long rivals of the Orsini, they produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-martin-v">Pope Martin V</a>, elected in 1417 to end the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Great Western Schism</a>, as well as many cardinals and commanders, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcantonio-colonna">Marcantonio Colonna</a>, who led the papal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galley">galleys</a> at Lepanto in 1571.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/colonna-family.jpg" alt="Colonna family" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ZuppaDiCarlo: blazon editing, Heralder: subjects · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stemma_della_famiglia_Colonna.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
